.\" The man page of the C++ port of the Claude Code CLI.
.TH "CC++" 1 "November 5, 2026" "claude-code-cpp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cc++ \- an interactive agent that writes and runs code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cc++
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ prompt ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cc++
is a command-line agent that reads a folder, answers questions about it and
changes it. It runs in an interactive session: the prompt is written at the
bottom of the screen, the answer of the model is written above it, and the
tools it asks for are run in between.
.PP
With a prompt of its own the session starts with that prompt and waits for
more. Without one it waits for the prompt.
.PP
The session keeps its conversation in a transcript under
.IR ~/.claude/projects/ ,
so that a session may be taken up again later with
.BR \-\-resume .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print
Print the response and exit, rather than opening a session.
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-format " fmt"
The format
.B \-\-print
writes in:
.B text
or
.BR json .
.TP
.BI \-\-model " model"
The model to use.
.TP
.BI \-\-fallback\-model " model"
The model to use when the primary one is unavailable.
.TP
.BI \-\-permission\-mode " mode"
How the session asks for permission:
.BR default ,
.BR acceptEdits ,
.BR plan ,
.B bypassPermissions
or
.BR dontAsk .
.TP
.B \-\-dangerously\-skip\-permissions
Skip all permission prompts. The session runs every tool it is asked for,
without asking.
.TP
.BI \-\-allowed\-tools " list"
The tools that need no approval, separated by commas.
.TP
.BI \-\-disallowed\-tools " list"
The tools that are never allowed, separated by commas.
.TP
.BI \-\-add\-dir " dir"
Add a working directory for this session.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-continue
Resume the most recent session.
.TP
.BI \-\-resume " [id]"
Resume a previous session. Without an id the sessions are listed and one of
them is picked.
.TP
.BI \-\-session\-id " id"
Use a specific session id.
.TP
.BI \-\-system\-prompt " text"
Replace the system prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-system\-prompt\-file " path"
Replace the system prompt with the contents of a file.
.TP
.BI \-\-append\-system\-prompt " text"
Append to the system prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-append\-system\-prompt\-file " path"
Append the contents of a file to the system prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-settings " json"
Settings overrides, as a JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-setting\-sources " list"
The setting sources to load.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print debug information.
.TP
.BI \-\-debug\-file " path"
Write debug information to a file.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print verbose output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help and exit.
.SH THE SESSION
The prompt of the session understands a few words of its own:
.B /help
opens the list of the commands,
.B /clear
drops the conversation,
.B /compact
writes a summary of it in place of the conversation itself,
.B /model
picks the model,
.B /config
opens the settings,
.B /mcp
opens the servers of MCP and
.B /exit
leaves the session.
.PP
A line that begins with
.B !
runs in the shell of the session and the model is asked about the result.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
The key of the API. The session asks for one when it is not there.
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL
The address of the API. A gateway of one's own may be named here.
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CODE_FULLSCREEN
Set it to
.B 1
to use the full-screen layout, the one that keeps the whole conversation on
the screen.
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER
The same as
.BR CLAUDE_CODE_FULLSCREEN .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.claude/settings.json
The settings of the user.
.TP
.I ~/.claude.json
The state of the machine: the theme, the trusted folders, the servers of MCP.
.TP
.I ./.claude/settings.json
The settings of the folder.
.TP
.I ./.mcp.json
The servers of MCP of the folder. They are only used when the folder is
trusted.
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects/
The transcripts of the sessions.
.SH SEE ALSO
The documentation of the reference:
.BR https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/overview
